  "doc": "I48 rename-reserved names (frozen at the I48 prereg; rule N1 (b) of tests_m4/test_eval_corpus.py). An identifier listed here for a language of the entry's files, or matching one of that language's patterns, is never renamed. Go: the keywords, the predeclared identifiers, _, init, main and C (cgo), and, by rule, the package-clause name of every Go file of the set (package_clause_names) and, in every Go file of the set that imports \"C\", every name X of a selector expression C.X (cgo_selector_names: cgo resolves C.X against the C preamble, so a declared Go name X is kept wherever it also names a C entity). Solidity: the keywords and reserved keywords, the units, every global name and member (msg.sender, x.length, x.slot, T.wrap, f.selector, type(T).interfaceId, abi.encodeCall, ...), _, Error and Panic (catch clauses), the EVM-Cancun Yul builtins and keywords, and the pragma words. The FunctionCallOptions names (value, gas, salt) and the contextual keywords (error, from, revert, global, transient, layout, at) are reserved too: they are valid identifiers in 0.8.24, but the renaming rewrites every token of a renamed word, keyword positions included (new C{salt: s}(), error E(), revert E(), using L for T global, ...), so renaming a variable named like one of them would break the keyword. A name declared by a dependency the checkout does not hold (lib/, node_modules/) is not listed: rule N1 (a) renames only names declared in the set, and the remaining risk is gap E-G3.",
